[gd_scene load_steps=28 format=3]

; CORAL COVE — the first official world (REQ-011), and deliberately built the
; way an outside contributor would build one: manifest + scene, NO scripts.
; Every mechanic below is a DECLARATION the game client's WorldSystems runtime
; binds — group membership plus node metadata, never code.
;
; THE ROUTE (one straight line down -Z, drivable with a single held forward
; key, because completability is a headless test, not a hope):
;
;   z   2  spawn (land — waddle)
;   z  -6  the lagoon: a WaterVolume across the route — water grammar
;   z -18  back onto land (grammar returns)                 [checkpoint 1]
;   z -22  HERMIT SNAIL — a discovery collectible (a rescued creature) on the
;          route, declared in the manifest, placed here, persisted by id
;   z -24  Glow Gill Mod pickup
;   z -28  GLOW GATE — a bioluminescent false wall, open only while the
;          equipped mod grants `reveal_bioluminescent`. Mandatory: it spans
;          the full route. (Camera hint volume tightens framing here.)
;   z -32  STRAY HOOK — an ORDINARY hazard (group `hazard`, capability leg):
;          it strips a leg with a pop and NEVER costs a life. On the route
;          on purpose, so every playthrough exercises pillar one.
;   z -34  Bubble Gill Mod pickup
;   z -38  BUBBLE GATE — open only while the mod grants `bubble_platform`.
;          Coral Cove gates on Bubble and Glow; Bubble Bay takes Jet, so the
;          official set covers all three MVP mods.       [checkpoint 2, -40]
;   z -41  REGEN STATION — regrows every lost capability (the leg comes back
;          before the seed bed, with a bloom).
;   z -42..-54  seven kelp seed pickups — the `kelp_seed` RESOURCE
;          collectible, declared once in the manifest and placed seven times;
;          each delivers to region `coral_shelf` (costs overridden to 3+4 via
;          sanctioned tuningOverrides, so the seventh seed completes it)
;   z -45  LANTERN SHRIMP — a second discovery collectible, OFF the route
;          (x +9): the optional branch the reward layer exists for. The
;          straight walk never touches it, and the walk asserts that.
;   z -56  SHELF WALL — the region's declared traversal gate; opens when
;          `coral_shelf` reaches `restored`. Restoration is MANDATORY.
;   z -60  finish volume — reach_volume returns the player to the lagoon.
;
; Below everything: a PIT VOLUME (group `pit_volume`) — CATASTROPHIC. Walking
; off the edge of the route costs a life and returns the player to the last
; checkpoint; at zero lives the count refills. That is the whole of the
; stakes layer, declared as one node.
;
; CHECKPOINT DENSITY follows REQ-003 AC-7: the replay from any anchor to the
; next must fit progression.max_retry_seconds (5 s) at normal traversal, so
; five checkpoints sit roughly every 10 m — z -10, -20, -30, -40, -50 — and
; the coral walk MEASURES every segment rather than trusting this comment.

